            row can be found using
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MimuraToda63"} Mimura-Toda 63
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 6
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 15
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k= 6,\ldots, 15
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=4,\ldots,8
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedic+Dictionary+of+Mathematics"} Encyclopedic Dictionary of Mathematics
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The table above equivalently corresponds to the lower-degree
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+K-theory"} unstable K-theory
              groups of spheres. In particular, this computes the homotopy groups:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo !
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_{2n} (U(n)) = U_n (S^{2n} ) = \mathbb{Z}/ n! \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              (see
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+K-theory"} there
              for more).
          %h3#in_infinite_dimension In infinite dimension
          %p
            A good discussion about the various topologies one might place on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
            and how they all agree and make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polish+space"} Polish
            group is in (
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe"}> Espinoza-Uribe
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathcal{H})
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %p
              Additionally,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathcal{H})
              for finite-dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gram-Schmidt+process"} Gram-Schmidt process
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Kuiper’s theorem)
            %p
              For a separable infinite-dimensional complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+topology"} norm topology
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuiper%27s+theorem"} Kuiper's theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
            is also contractible in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+operator+topology"} strong operator topology
            (due to Dixmier and Douady).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This in contrast to the finite dimensional situation. For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \ge 1
              ),
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
              is not contractible.
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(n)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to B U(n) \hookrightarrow B U(n+1) \hookrightarrow B U(n+2) \to \cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+limit"} direct limit
            over this is written
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                    %mi n
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B U := {\lim_\to}_n B U(n)
          %p
            or sometimes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(\infty)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(\mathcal{H})
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            an infinite-dimensional Hilbert space. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            for more on this.
          %h3#SUn Relation to special unitary group
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} split
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SU(n) \to U(n) \to U(1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U(n) \simeq SU(n) \rtimes U(1)
                    \\,.
          %h3#RelationToOrthogonalSymplecticAndGeneralLinearGroup Relation to orthogonal, symplectic and general linear group
          %p
            The unitary group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(2n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(2n,\mathbb{R})
            and the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{C})
            inside the real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(2n,\mathbb{R})
          %p Actually it is already the intersection of any two of these three, a fact also known as the “2 out of 3-property” of the unitary group.
          %p
            This intersection property makes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(n)
            (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+Hermitian+structure"} almost Hermitian structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+symplectic+structure"} almost symplectic structure
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structure"} first-order integrable case
            this is precisely a joint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            structure),
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          %h3#coset_spaces Coset spaces
          #nSphereAsUnitaryCosetSpace.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} (2n+1)-spheres
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
              of unitary groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{2n+1} \simeq U(n+1)/U(n)
                    \\,.
          #ComplexStiefelManifold.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \leq k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_n(\mathbb{C}^k) \coloneqq U(k)/U(k-n)
            %p
              is called the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %em
                complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel+manifold"} Stiefel manifold
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^k
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel+manifold"} Stiefel manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_n(\mathbb{C}^k)
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComplexStiefelManifold"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+topological+space"} 2(k-n)-connected
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U(k-n)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    U(k)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    U(k)/U(k-n)
                    \=
                    V_n(\mathbb{C}^k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnitaryGroupIsCompact"}
              and by
              %a{:href => "QuotientProjectionForCompactLieSubgroupIsPrincipal"} this corollary
              the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(k)\to U(k)/U(k-n)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              of this
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfUnitaryGroupnIntoUnitaryGroupnPlusIneIsnMinus1Equivalence"}
              it has the following form in degrees bounded by
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi epi
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    \\pi_{\bullet \leq 2(k-n)}(U(k-n))
                    \\overset{epi}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_{\bullet \leq 2(k-n)}(U(k))
                    \\overset{0}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_{\bullet \leq 2(k-n)}(V_n(\mathbb{C}^k))
                    \\overset{0}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_{\bullet-1 \lt 2(k-n)}(U(k))
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_{\bullet-1 \lt 2(k-n)}(U(k-n))
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
            %p This implies the claim.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+unitary+group"} stable unitary group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
            %li
              %p
                The subgroup of unitary matrices with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
                equal to 1 is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} center
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+unitary+group"} projective unitary group
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+product+of+circles"} symmetric product of circles
            %li
              %p
                The analog of the unitary group for real metric spaces is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            %li
              %p
                similarly:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+unitary+group"} quaternionic unitary group
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+Lie+algebra"} unitary Lie algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
          %h2#references References
          %p (…)
          %ul
